{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners feels like a natural next choice because polished vocal duets and standards connect with my interest in musical theatre and expressive singers.",
    "25 offers the heartfelt ballads I want today, while Eagles: The Very Best Of appeals through warm harmonies and easygoing melodies."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Hybrid Theory, St. Anger and Fallen emphasize heavy guitars and intensity when I am looking for soothing melodies and voices I can settle into.",
    "The Endless River may offer relaxed listening, but instrumental rock does not satisfy the same interest that drew me to relaxing classical music."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The list seems to assume that familiar albums are appealing to me regardless of their sound or singing style.",
    "It treats atmospheric or mellow rock as interchangeable with the classical music and vocal performances I have recently chosen."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My choices of Stages, A Musical Affair and Lead With Your Heart suggest that expressive, polished vocal performances matter more to me than broad familiarity.",
    "My latest interest in relaxing classical music points toward gentler listening today; even appealing choices like Adele 21 and The Beatles 1 can wait when another album fits my immediate mood better."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my taste for melodic singing, but miss how strongly gentle arrangements and polished vocal performances guide my choices today."
}"}
